From: Max <max@maxnet.lan>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 01:50:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] net: usb: rndis_host: support SuperSpeed multi-packet aggregation

In SuperSpeed (5Gbps) USB 3.0 mode, modern Android devices aggregate multiple
network frames per bulk IN transfer. With default 2048-byte URBs, batched transfers
cause buffer overruns and xHCI TRB dequeuer faults under heavy throughput (such
as speed tests).

Increase dev->rx_urb_size to 32KB when operating at USB_SPEED_SUPER or higher,
and 16KB otherwise. Also ignore empty 0-byte URBs to prevent bogus rx_errors.

Signed-off-by: Max <max@maxnet.lan>
---
--- a/drivers/net/usb/rndis_host.c
+++ b/drivers/net/usb/rndis_host.c
@@ -344,6 +344,12 @@ generic_rndis_bind(struct usbnet *dev, s
 
 	dev->rx_urb_size = dev->hard_mtu + (dev->maxpacket + 1);
 	dev->rx_urb_size &= ~(dev->maxpacket - 1);
+
+	/* SuperSpeed devices require larger RX URBs for packet aggregation */
+	if (dev->udev->speed >= USB_SPEED_SUPER)
+		dev->rx_urb_size = max_t(size_t, dev->rx_urb_size, 32 * 1024);
+	else
+		dev->rx_urb_size = max_t(size_t, dev->rx_urb_size, 16 * 1024);
 	u.init->max_transfer_size = cpu_to_le32(dev->rx_urb_size);
 
 	net->netdev_ops = &rndis_netdev_ops;
@@ -495,6 +501,9 @@ int rndis_rx_fixup(struct usbnet *dev, s
 {
 	bool dst_mac_fixup;
 
+	if (skb->len == 0)
+		return 1;
+
 	/* This check is no longer done by usbnet */
 	if (skb->len < dev->net->hard_header_len)
 		return 0;
